  "question": {
    "text": "If $R$ be the set of all real numbers and $f: R \\rightarrow R$ is given by $f(x)=3 x^{2}+1$. Then, the set $f^{-1}([1,6])$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HlEyO",
      "text": "$\\left\\{-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}, 0, \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}\\right\\}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8KcjG",
      "text": "$\\left[-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}, \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mqg34",
      "text": "$\\left[-\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}, \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}\\right]$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zHmI7",
      "text": "$\\left(-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}, \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}\\right)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $f(x)=3 x^{2}+1$\r\nLet $\\quad y=3 x^{2}+1$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 3 x^{2}=y-1 \\Rightarrow x^{2}=\\frac{y-1}{3}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{y-1}{3}}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad f^{-1}(x)=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{x-1}{3}}$\r\nWhen $x \\in[1,6]$\r\nThen, $\\quad f^{-1}(x) \\in\\left[-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}, \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}\\right]$",
    "image": null
  },
